(1231727, 155265, 26475, '<td valign="top">most likely, the orange is acurate, but pulling it out of the picture by desaturating everything else does nothing for the image, aside from making it jaring to look at.  I don''t think it was necessary for this piece that otherwise would have been wonderful, I''m sure.</td>', 'most likely, the orange is acurate, but pulling it out of the picture by desaturating everything else does nothing for the image, aside from making it jaring to look at.  I don''t think it was necessary for this piece that otherwise would have been wonderful, I''m sure.', '2005-03-16 10:08:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231733, 155559, 6999, '<td valign="top">Oh, bu this is wonderfully composed, and a marvellous approach to the challenge. It''s complex, graceful, and shows real mastery of the graphic elements of composition. The figures are placed perfectly for the balance of the shot .. but I really wonder about the motion blur ... such a minor complaint though. Excellent.</td>', 'Oh, bu this is wonderfully composed, and a marvellous approach to the challenge. It''s complex, graceful, and shows real mastery of the graphic elements of composition. The figures are placed perfectly for the balance of the shot .. but I really wonder about the motion blur ... such a minor complaint though. Excellent.', '2005-03-16 10:10:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231745, 154949, 6999, '<td valign="top">Seems unneccesarily noisy for a simple composition, and is a bit chaotic in it''s placement of elements.</td>', 'Seems unneccesarily noisy for a simple composition, and is a bit chaotic in it''s placement of elements.', '2005-03-16 10:12:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231755, 155460, 6999, '<td valign="top">I don''t see that the noise generally and the sharpening artefacts (particularly around the point of the pencil) are of any great help to this image. The extreme shallowness of the depth of field suggests a large-sensor camera, and yet the final image''s uqality suggests something much less sophisticated.</td>', 'I don''t see that the noise generally and the sharpening artefacts (particularly around the point of the pencil) are of any great help to this image. The extreme shallowness of the depth of field suggests a large-sensor camera, and yet the final image''s uqality suggests something much less sophisticated.', '2005-03-16 10:15:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231968, 155394, 34192, '<td valign="top">like the title.  Can''t wait til we have those here - then I''ll know its spring.  Focus and DOF good for subject. composition interesting. 7</td>', 'like the title.  Can''t wait til we have those here - then I''ll know its spring.  Focus and DOF good for subject. composition interesting. 7', '2005-03-16 11:24:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231971, 155746, 6804, '<td valign="top">To me;  this entry represents everything I love about photography.  To pull the viewer into a place they''ve never been and have them reminiscing about a time in their life when they were at just such a place.  The dirt road seems almost symbolic of harder times but when looking back down that road the mind can see only the beauty and charm of life''s journey.  <br/> <br/>The lighting could not have been better to create the almost "drops of sunlight" in the trees.  Your color choice is just perfect for keeping this timeless.  These are all the things I aspire to as a photographer.  Congratulations on not only my highest rated picture of the challenge, but one of my all time favorite images on DPC.  This is simply a stunning capture in the middle of a daydream.</td>', 'To me;  this entry represents everything I love about photography.  To pull the viewer into a place they''ve never been and have them reminiscing about a time in their life when they were at just such a place.  The dirt road seems almost symbolic of harder times but when looking back down that road the mind can see only the beauty and charm of life''s journey.   The lighting could not have been better to create the almost "drops of sunlight" in the trees.  Your color choice is just perfect for keeping this timeless.  These are all the things I aspire to as a photographer.  Congratulations on not only my highest rated picture of the challenge, but one of my all time favorite images on DPC.  This is simply a stunning capture in the middle of a daydream.', '2005-03-16 11:25:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231981, 155483, 29797, '<td valign="top">The rotation and flow of the lines really works here. Very cool shot.</td>', 'The rotation and flow of the lines really works here. Very cool shot.', '2005-03-16 11:33:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231994, 155255, 29797, '<td valign="top">REALLY nice and simple shot. I went up to the poppies the day after you guys, but it was too windy for any shot like this : (</td>', 'REALLY nice and simple shot. I went up to the poppies the day after you guys, but it was too windy for any shot like this : (', '2005-03-16 11:39:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(1231995, 155461, 14386, '<td valign="top">A classic.  Both the picture and the model.  She has an expression of charming resignation.  Shy and coy yet the wisdom in her face is very evident.  I like the fact that she''s not looking at you as she seemed detached from the world and makes her float astral...background enhances the focus in her face.<br/> <br/></td>', 'A classic.  Both the picture and the model.  She has an expression of charming resignation.  Shy and coy yet the wisdom in her face is very evident.  I like the fact that she''s not looking at you as she seemed detached from the world and makes her float astral...background enhances the focus in her face. ', '2005-03-16 11:40:08.000000', NULL, 1),
