(1232465, 155411, 2490, '<td valign="top">EXCELLENT bw!  Too bad about the blurry hand; I''m betting its a tremor??8</td>', 'EXCELLENT bw!  Too bad about the blurry hand; I''m betting its a tremor??8', '2005-03-16 14:31:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232485, 155555, 2490, '<td valign="top">This is one of very few 10s...  I call this the winner.</td>', 'This is one of very few 10s...  I call this the winner.', '2005-03-16 14:37:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232486, 154698, 2490, '<td valign="top">Excellent road shot! 9</td>', 'Excellent road shot! 9', '2005-03-16 14:38:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232487, 155639, 2490, '<td valign="top">Now this is excellently creative. Also well done.  9.</td>', 'Now this is excellently creative. Also well done.  9.', '2005-03-16 14:38:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232546, 155747, 33210, '<td valign="top">nice shot good composition &amp; DOF</td>', 'nice shot good composition & DOF', '2005-03-16 15:03:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232568, 154859, 6870, '<td valign="top">Sure! Nice lines, and a very interesting expression, giving the lines ambiguous meaning. 9</td>', 'Sure! Nice lines, and a very interesting expression, giving the lines ambiguous meaning. 9', '2005-03-16 15:14:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232571, 154064, 6870, '<td valign="top">I like the blur here a lot. Fun point of view, and the asymmetrical lighting works well for me. 9</td>', 'I like the blur here a lot. Fun point of view, and the asymmetrical lighting works well for me. 9', '2005-03-16 15:15:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232577, 155209, 6870, '<td valign="top">This is a great idea. The lines of the fields are good subjects, as you''ve noticed! The way they lead to the house or barn is nice, too. I laso like how the house is just below half way down. This is really out of focus, though, and a bit overexposed. You''ll probably want to check that next time.</td>', 'This is a great idea. The lines of the fields are good subjects, as you''ve noticed! The way they lead to the house or barn is nice, too. I laso like how the house is just below half way down. This is really out of focus, though, and a bit overexposed. You''ll probably want to check that next time.', '2005-03-16 15:16:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232580, 155725, 6870, '<td valign="top">Classic capture, competently done. 8</td>', 'Classic capture, competently done. 8', '2005-03-16 15:17:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232584, 155758, 6870, '<td valign="top">Have you tried this in b/w? I t hink it would really do well. Nice point of view. Dark, but I like it that way.7</td>', 'Have you tried this in b/w? I t hink it would really do well. Nice point of view. Dark, but I like it that way.7', '2005-03-16 15:18:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232610, 155634, 13749, '<td valign="top">very nice, but leaves me craving more sharpness (i hope it''s not my monitor), as the edges seem ever so slightly undefined at times. 7.</td>', 'very nice, but leaves me craving more sharpness (i hope it''s not my monitor), as the edges seem ever so slightly undefined at times. 7.', '2005-03-16 15:32:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232682, 155765, 6999, '<td valign="top">To my eye, something doesn''t work here: though it''s quite difficult to say what, exactly. Compositionally, perhaps your vanishing point could be more strongly placed in frame, rather than this halfway house between central and privileged on a thirds line. I''m also not sure the colours work well - that beige colour of tthe metalwork is rather neutral and uninteresting, and the brown is quite lifeless too: did you think about making this a monochrome image? The structure itself is very regular, which usually works better with a perfectly regular view of it, compositionally. Your slightly off-centred point of view adds an almost subconscious sense of disturbance to that regularity, and I don''t think that helps either. There is a conflict between the very simple elements of the bridge in the upper part of frame - simple geometrical structures, beams and uprights against a clear blue - and the boards and lower area, where the lines become more chaotic and complicated. It''s like two diffrent ideas of an image together, and that also makes it a tricky picture to appreciate on any one level. I think perhaps the question is, ''which part of this structure was it that really interested you?'' - enough to shoot it with the evident care you have put into this. <br/> <br/>After all this, I think it is that tension between the simplicity of the upper part of frame, and the complexity of the lower that most hurts this image: I''ve tried looking at the upper third (or so) and the lower two thirds (or so) separately (just by framing with the window), and i think what you have is a joining of two quite strong images in such a way that the impact of either is somewhat taken away. <br/> <br/>Technically, of course there are a lot of strong things here: focus, presentation (I mean compression, and colour rendition) are absolutely fine, and there is strong detail present - the smoothness of the metalwork comes out, and that kind of texture is an element many people struggle with.</td>', 'To my eye, something doesn''t work here: though it''s quite difficult to say what, exactly. Compositionally, perhaps your vanishing point could be more strongly placed in frame, rather than this halfway house between central and privileged on a thirds line. I''m also not sure the colours work well - that beige colour of tthe metalwork is rather neutral and uninteresting, and the brown is quite lifeless too: did you think about making this a monochrome image? The structure itself is very regular, which usually works better with a perfectly regular view of it, compositionally. Your slightly off-centred point of view adds an almost subconscious sense of disturbance to that regularity, and I don''t think that helps either. There is a conflict between the very simple elements of the bridge in the upper part of frame - simple geometrical structures, beams and uprights against a clear blue - and the boards and lower area, where the lines become more chaotic and complicated. It''s like two diffrent ideas of an image together, and that also makes it a tricky picture to appreciate on any one level. I think perhaps the question is, ''which part of this structure was it that really interested you?'' - enough to shoot it with the evident care you have put into this.  After all this, I think it is that tension between the simplicity of the upper part of frame, and the complexity of the lower that most hurts this image: I''ve tried looking at the upper third (or so) and the lower two thirds (or so) separately (just by framing with the window), and i think what you have is a joining of two quite strong images in such a way that the impact of either is somewhat taken away.  Technically, of course there are a lot of strong things here: focus, presentation (I mean compression, and colour rendition) are absolutely fine, and there is strong detail present - the smoothness of the metalwork comes out, and that kind of texture is an element many people struggle with.', '2005-03-16 16:03:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232692, 155188, 6999, '<td valign="top">The picking out of that reverse angled thread is quite impressive. The image as a whole is for me let down by the sudden shift in complexity of the water in the top third of frame, I think. For such a very simple and elegant composition, it really harms the gentle and reflective mood of the scene.</td>', 'The picking out of that reverse angled thread is quite impressive. The image as a whole is for me let down by the sudden shift in complexity of the water in the top third of frame, I think. For such a very simple and elegant composition, it really harms the gentle and reflective mood of the scene.', '2005-03-16 16:09:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232701, 155534, 6999, '<td valign="top">There is strength in this image. However, your vanishing pont could for me happily have been placed higher in your frame - the point you''ve chosen feels quite weak compositionally; and the extreme contrast of the scene with that light isn''t really helped by the use of colour, I think: there''s no real depth to the tones that remain, and the movement from shadow to brighness is too quick, generally. That contrast lends itself so much more strongly to the use of black and white. This is also a heavily compressed image, resulting in that blockiness in the sky - you have three times as much data available to use as this, and it almost always hurts not to use it. It''s an ideal scene for the challenge though, and the detailing and focus are good.</td>', 'There is strength in this image. However, your vanishing pont could for me happily have been placed higher in your frame - the point you''ve chosen feels quite weak compositionally; and the extreme contrast of the scene with that light isn''t really helped by the use of colour, I think: there''s no real depth to the tones that remain, and the movement from shadow to brighness is too quick, generally. That contrast lends itself so much more strongly to the use of black and white. This is also a heavily compressed image, resulting in that blockiness in the sky - you have three times as much data available to use as this, and it almost always hurts not to use it. It''s an ideal scene for the challenge though, and the detailing and focus are good.', '2005-03-16 16:13:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232716, 155395, 28592, '<td valign="top">Funny... because it''s true ;-)</td>', 'Funny... because it''s true ;-)', '2005-03-16 16:21:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232728, 155129, 28592, '<td valign="top">Nice and clean.  I like this one.</td>', 'Nice and clean.  I like this one.', '2005-03-16 16:25:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232740, 155427, 28592, '<td valign="top">I don''t know what to say, but there is something about it that I like wery much - good job.</td>', 'I don''t know what to say, but there is something about it that I like wery much - good job.', '2005-03-16 16:30:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232770, 155222, 3087, '<td valign="top">THIS is COOL!</td>', 'THIS is COOL!', '2005-03-16 16:44:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232773, 155048, 3087, '<td valign="top">Nice abstract feel; strong composition; mix of hard black and white with softer, warmer colours and textures works well.</td>', 'Nice abstract feel; strong composition; mix of hard black and white with softer, warmer colours and textures works well.', '2005-03-16 16:45:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232791, 155159, 6999, '<td valign="top">In Black and Whie this could almost be a Tony Ray-Jone photograph. Aren''t people strange?</td>', 'In Black and Whie this could almost be a Tony Ray-Jone photograph. Aren''t people strange?', '2005-03-16 16:50:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232803, 153666, 3087, '<td valign="top">Wow! What an absolutely marvellous sense of perspective and scale!</td>', 'Wow! What an absolutely marvellous sense of perspective and scale!', '2005-03-16 16:51:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232804, 155411, 28592, '<td valign="top">A winner?</td>', 'A winner?', '2005-03-16 16:52:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232806, 154041, 3087, '<td valign="top">Man, I''m such a sucker for shallow DOF when used well... as it is here.</td>', 'Man, I''m such a sucker for shallow DOF when used well... as it is here.', '2005-03-16 16:52:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232812, 155411, 3087, '<td valign="top">Wonderful subject, great composition, works perfectly in black and white. Focus feels a touch soft on his face but I''m assuming it''s not as his hair seems sharp. I like the motion in his hand.</td>', 'Wonderful subject, great composition, works perfectly in black and white. Focus feels a touch soft on his face but I''m assuming it''s not as his hair seems sharp. I like the motion in his hand.', '2005-03-16 16:53:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232815, 154127, 3087, '<td valign="top">Quite haunting. I wonder if it would have been better as a duotoned black and white or just with a touch of the saturation taken out of the sky?</td>', 'Quite haunting. I wonder if it would have been better as a duotoned black and white or just with a touch of the saturation taken out of the sky?', '2005-03-16 16:54:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232816, 154715, 3087, '<td valign="top">Beautiful detail, nice DOF choice, excellent close crop. Black and white perfect to bring out shapes, lines and tones.</td>', 'Beautiful detail, nice DOF choice, excellent close crop. Black and white perfect to bring out shapes, lines and tones.', '2005-03-16 16:54:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232820, 155486, 3087, '<td valign="top">I seldom appreciate selective desaturation as it''s so often done for the sake of using the technique and the item left in colour is not the main point of focus/ subject. Here it works superbly to concentrate the attention on the lines as well as their lovely rich colour. Works really well for me. Nice low viewpoint.</td>', 'I seldom appreciate selective desaturation as it''s so often done for the sake of using the technique and the item left in colour is not the main point of focus/ subject. Here it works superbly to concentrate the attention on the lines as well as their lovely rich colour. Works really well for me. Nice low viewpoint.', '2005-03-16 16:56:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232822, 155198, 3087, '<td valign="top">Almost Yin and Yang. Lovely use of light and shadow. Central composition works wonderfully well. Beautiful texture. Muted colours. Lovely!</td>', 'Almost Yin and Yang. Lovely use of light and shadow. Central composition works wonderfully well. Beautiful texture. Muted colours. Lovely!', '2005-03-16 16:58:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232826, 155461, 3087, '<td valign="top">This is the interpretation I idly thought about trying to convey but I couldn''t think of a suitable model and I know I''d not have created as compelling an image as you have here. Even without eye contact you''ve created a connection, a sympathetic reaction, a curiousity about the subject and her life experiences. Nicely composed too.</td>', 'This is the interpretation I idly thought about trying to convey but I couldn''t think of a suitable model and I know I''d not have created as compelling an image as you have here. Even without eye contact you''ve created a connection, a sympathetic reaction, a curiousity about the subject and her life experiences. Nicely composed too.', '2005-03-16 16:59:42.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232828, 155474, 3087, '<td valign="top">As already mentioned in person, needs to be much sharper in focus with a touch more contrast too. But I really do like the abstract nature and texture that you almost have here.</td>', 'As already mentioned in person, needs to be much sharper in focus with a touch more contrast too. But I really do like the abstract nature and texture that you almost have here.', '2005-03-16 17:00:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232830, 155520, 3087, '<td valign="top">Fantastic composition. The frame itself feels like the enclosing walls of a small room. The almost silhouetted presentation of the model works well. I like the green tones. And lots of wonderful lines and textures.</td>', 'Fantastic composition. The frame itself feels like the enclosing walls of a small room. The almost silhouetted presentation of the model works well. I like the green tones. And lots of wonderful lines and textures.', '2005-03-16 17:01:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232846, 154572, 22046, '<td valign="top">I love all the secondary lines in this. The lit up inside, the rows of shadow lines on the rings, and the bright solic outside lines on each ring. Beautiful color too. One of my favorites!</td>', 'I love all the secondary lines in this. The lit up inside, the rows of shadow lines on the rings, and the bright solic outside lines on each ring. Beautiful color too. One of my favorites!', '2005-03-16 17:15:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232854, 155579, 26679, '<td valign="top">In the UK a fanny is on the opposite side to this image.....<br/>However I like the idea here...</td>', 'In the UK a fanny is on the opposite side to this image.....However I like the idea here...', '2005-03-16 17:17:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232967, 155498, 10080, '<td valign="top">beautifull done! 10</td>', 'beautifull done! 10', '2005-03-16 18:11:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(1232988, 154572, 33435, '<td valign="top">I originally gave this a 9, bumping to 10, nice work.</td>', 'I originally gave this a 9, bumping to 10, nice work.', '2005-03-16 18:20:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233021, 155676, 11248, '<td valign="top">They are so cute. The lines give perspective to the picture. Personnally I find the light a bit harsh at the right. Still one of my preferred in this challenge.<br/></td>', 'They are so cute. The lines give perspective to the picture. Personnally I find the light a bit harsh at the right. Still one of my preferred in this challenge.', '2005-03-16 18:38:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233023, 155520, 11248, '<td valign="top">One of the few pictures that exploits the lines at it max. The contrast between the cold straight lines and the warm curves is absolutely fantastic. Very good work - 10</td>', 'One of the few pictures that exploits the lines at it max. The contrast between the cold straight lines and the warm curves is absolutely fantastic. Very good work - 10', '2005-03-16 18:40:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233025, 155373, 11248, '<td valign="top">The contrast between the hard wires and the softness of the lines on the butterfly wings is very interresting. One of my preferred shot. -9</td>', 'The contrast between the hard wires and the softness of the lines on the butterfly wings is very interresting. One of my preferred shot. -9', '2005-03-16 18:41:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233033, 155746, 11248, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. The lines are very attractive and let the viewer with the question: What will i find at the end of the road. Very good work. -8</td>', 'Beautiful. The lines are very attractive and let the viewer with the question: What will i find at the end of the road. Very good work. -8', '2005-03-16 18:44:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233036, 153594, 19035, '<td valign="top">Good subject matter, the lower left part of the palm leaf comes off a bit too bright, but this is a still a good photo.  6.</td>', 'Good subject matter, the lower left part of the palm leaf comes off a bit too bright, but this is a still a good photo.  6.', '2005-03-16 18:47:34.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233037, 155255, 19035, '<td valign="top">Pretty flower, I wish it was a little closer in to see more details on the petals.</td>', 'Pretty flower, I wish it was a little closer in to see more details on the petals.', '2005-03-16 18:48:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233043, 155226, 19035, '<td valign="top">Almost an abstract , nicely composed.  Would be interesting to see this in Black and White</td>', 'Almost an abstract , nicely composed.  Would be interesting to see this in Black and White', '2005-03-16 18:49:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233045, 155587, 19035, '<td valign="top">Well done, great colors and balance, bumping up to a 7.</td>', 'Well done, great colors and balance, bumping up to a 7.', '2005-03-16 18:50:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233046, 155373, 19035, '<td valign="top">Beautiful subject matter and depth of focus.</td>', 'Beautiful subject matter and depth of focus.', '2005-03-16 18:50:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233048, 155427, 19035, '<td valign="top">The white areas are a bit too bright for me, but this is a good idea and has promise.</td>', 'The white areas are a bit too bright for me, but this is a good idea and has promise.', '2005-03-16 18:52:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233049, 155129, 19035, '<td valign="top">Simple but effective picture, nice colors.</td>', 'Simple but effective picture, nice colors.', '2005-03-16 18:52:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(1233082, 155520, 8860, '<td valign="top">Very graphic shot - good colour and crispness. But where the hell are the lines??????????<br/> <br/>I can''t help noticing that she has a rather nice figure too.<br/>; )</td>', 'Very graphic shot - good colour and crispness. But where the hell are the lines?????????? I can''t help noticing that she has a rather nice figure too.; )', '2005-03-16 19:21:27.000000', NULL, 1),
