(1237302, 155044, 34192, '<td valign="top">I would have removed the staple.  Because of its uniqueness in a repeated pattern it draws my eye.  And I wonder why the staple is important in the image.  Since I think the pattern rather than the staple should be the focus, this loses 1 for composition.  Focus and color are excellent. 6</td>', 'I would have removed the staple.  Because of its uniqueness in a repeated pattern it draws my eye.  And I wonder why the staple is important in the image.  Since I think the pattern rather than the staple should be the focus, this loses 1 for composition.  Focus and color are excellent. 6', '2005-03-19 06:51:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1237303, 155265, 19978, '<td valign="top">This is a tremendous image in composition. The lines are beautifully used throughout. The selective desat looks as though it has had some bad results in the small vertical cables, which look blotchy halfway up on the right. If not for that, I believe you''d have a very highly placed photo.</td>', 'This is a tremendous image in composition. The lines are beautifully used throughout. The selective desat looks as though it has had some bad results in the small vertical cables, which look blotchy halfway up on the right. If not for that, I believe you''d have a very highly placed photo.', '2005-03-19 06:53:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(1237305, 155729, 19978, '<td valign="top">An absolutely GREAT idea for this challenge, and I think you''ve pulled it off brilliantly. The court lines and colors are sharp and bright, and the ball has just the right amount of blur to suggest that it''s an actual freeze-frame from the US Open where Agassi got a bad call (or whatever). My biggest complaint is that you thought of this and not me. Bravo and kudos. I hope you score highly with this.</td>', 'An absolutely GREAT idea for this challenge, and I think you''ve pulled it off brilliantly. The court lines and colors are sharp and bright, and the ball has just the right amount of blur to suggest that it''s an actual freeze-frame from the US Open where Agassi got a bad call (or whatever). My biggest complaint is that you thought of this and not me. Bravo and kudos. I hope you score highly with this.', '2005-03-19 06:55:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(1237306, 155669, 34192, '<td valign="top">the brown in this picture does not work for me.  The focus of the image would stand out more if the POV was from a little more to the left.  This would move the focused stamen (?)  in front of the background making it stand out more.  Changing the POV would also get the other stamens (?) a little more out of focus.  Its interesting (kind of) but doesn''t really hold my attention.</td>', 'the brown in this picture does not work for me.  The focus of the image would stand out more if the POV was from a little more to the left.  This would move the focused stamen (?)  in front of the background making it stand out more.  Changing the POV would also get the other stamens (?) a little more out of focus.  Its interesting (kind of) but doesn''t really hold my attention.', '2005-03-19 06:57:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(1237308, 155618, 34192, '<td valign="top">I found this image interesting.  The subject is boring but the composition makes up for it, as does the focus and POV. Well done crop. I think this is probably the best of the powerlines images. 8</td>', 'I found this image interesting.  The subject is boring but the composition makes up for it, as does the focus and POV. Well done crop. I think this is probably the best of the powerlines images. 8', '2005-03-19 07:00:29.000000', NULL, 1),
