(1241964, 155094, 25388, '<td valign="top">You depicted the reality and illusion of "Lines" with ingenuity and excellence; congratulations on the thought, the construction, and the photography of an outstanding entry; yours had my highest vote and should have been in the 7''s IMO. Regards, Dave</td>', 'You depicted the reality and illusion of "Lines" with ingenuity and excellence; congratulations on the thought, the construction, and the photography of an outstanding entry; yours had my highest vote and should have been in the 7''s IMO. Regards, Dave', '2005-03-21 20:58:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(1241971, 154127, 7033, '<td valign="top">Very nicely captured, David!  In spite of my interest in trains (and particularly Utah''s place in the completion of the transcontinental railroad) this is one location I have yet to visit.  My wife''s great-uncle worked in the quarry where the SP obtained the rock for the causeway that put the trestle out to pasture.  I was aware of Trestlewood''s efforts to salvage the old timber from the cutoff, but had assumed their work was completed and the trestle was no longer there.  Looks like I''ve got a road trip to take!</td>', 'Very nicely captured, David!  In spite of my interest in trains (and particularly Utah''s place in the completion of the transcontinental railroad) this is one location I have yet to visit.  My wife''s great-uncle worked in the quarry where the SP obtained the rock for the causeway that put the trestle out to pasture.  I was aware of Trestlewood''s efforts to salvage the old timber from the cutoff, but had assumed their work was completed and the trestle was no longer there.  Looks like I''ve got a road trip to take!', '2005-03-21 21:01:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(1241983, 155461, 9452, '<td valign="top">Congratulations! I love this image, and I am glad that a non superphotoshoped image got a ribbon!<br/> <br/>Thank you!</td>', 'Congratulations! I love this image, and I am glad that a non superphotoshoped image got a ribbon! Thank you!', '2005-03-21 21:07:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(1242088, 155634, 6073, '<td valign="top">Here''s the color version --&gt; <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=158630" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6073/thumb/158630.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6073/thumb/158630.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/6073/thumb/158630.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Here''s the color version --> ', '2005-03-21 22:12:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(1242098, 155719, 20462, '<td valign="top">Abstract photos tend to get voted a lot lower for reasons that are beyond me.  Abstract lines that are not necessarily abstract could be construed to be so, if the context of the photo is not portrayed through the capture.  Meaning, I personally take to abstract, but a lot of people do not.  If you want higher votes, stay a little farther away from pictures that people can''t decipher what they are looking at.  This is your first challenge, so the learning curve might be steep, but you will rise fast.  Check out my first couple of challenges versus what I am submitting now.  As for my part, in two months I can already feel a big difference.  So in my opinion, don''t give up on the site, because it has taught me a ton of technique, process and thought.  Hope that is enough of a comment for you.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-03-21 22:21:24.</i></td>', 'Abstract photos tend to get voted a lot lower for reasons that are beyond me.  Abstract lines that are not necessarily abstract could be construed to be so, if the context of the photo is not portrayed through the capture.  Meaning, I personally take to abstract, but a lot of people do not.  If you want higher votes, stay a little farther away from pictures that people can''t decipher what they are looking at.  This is your first challenge, so the learning curve might be steep, but you will rise fast.  Check out my first couple of challenges versus what I am submitting now.  As for my part, in two months I can already feel a big difference.  So in my opinion, don''t give up on the site, because it has taught me a ton of technique, process and thought.  Hope that is enough of a comment for you.', '2005-03-21 22:15:58.000000', '2005-03-21 22:21:24.000000', 0),
(1242136, 154893, 6349, '<td valign="top">missed this challenge, would have given this a 10.  I got so excited looking at this because I always wanted to try this effect but never had a camera that could do it.  I think my new one does! (of course I won''t get any results nearly this good)  :)</td>', 'missed this challenge, would have given this a 10.  I got so excited looking at this because I always wanted to try this effect but never had a camera that could do it.  I think my new one does! (of course I won''t get any results nearly this good)  :)', '2005-03-21 22:27:55.000000', NULL, 0),
